      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Every individual’s body reacts differently, and even small quantities of potassium can be significant for someone with CKD. The kidneys' filtering capability is impaired, so the body handles potassium less effectively. While 99mg seems modest, your best course of action is still to speak with a healthcare professional who's familiar with your case. Even a one-time increased dose could pose a risk and they would help ascertain if it's safe to proceed, or suggest alternative measures while you wait for your appointment. It's always better to err on the side of caution.",
